#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124212 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c2d581-8b12-575d-bb78-d8bb293a7339" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Sphere or Ellipsoid"}] :question/id #uuid "3344e23f-56eb-5880-b1cd-7198525daf91" :question/math-academy-id "e-12554" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\dfrac {x^2} {4} +  \\dfrac {y^2} 9  + z^2 = 1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the ellipsoid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+{z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} \\\\ z & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the interior of the ellipse $\\dfrac {x^2} {4} +  \\dfrac {y^2} 9 =  1$ and its boundary.  \n\nTherefore, the domain is of $z = z(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\bigg\\{ (x, y) \\,:\\, \\dfrac {x^2} {4} +  \\dfrac {y^2} 9 \\leq  1 \\bigg\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124311 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124502 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Intercepts of Spheres and Ellipsoids"}] :question/id #uuid "ca62112b-9989-5ede-9cbf-561f5dc2ba43" :question/math-academy-id "e-5263" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\dfrac {(x-2)^2} {2} +  {y^2} + \\dfrac{(z+1)^2}{2} =1,$ find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+(0)^{2}+\\frac{(0+1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =1,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $\\left(1, 0, 0\\right)$ and $\\left(3, 0, 0\\right).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124315 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124506 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "304a85ac-e980-5081-8f2b-20df471c30fc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Center and Radius of a Sphere"}] :question/id #uuid "8db4fc0c-416b-57a4-8612-a422a7681076" :question/math-academy-id "e-5311" :question/problem "What are the radius $r$ and the coordinates of the center $C$ for the sphere $(x+1)^2 + y^2 + z^2 + 8z = 20?$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of a sphere centered at $(x_0, y_0, z_0)$ with radius $r > 0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-x_0)^2 + (y-y_0)^2 + (z-z_0)^2 = r^2.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $z$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+8z & =20 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+({z}^{2}+8z+16) & =20+16 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z+4)^{2} & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-(-1))^2 + (y-0)^2 + (z-(-4))^2 = 6^2,\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the center at the point $C(-1,0,-4)$ and the radius $r=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124316 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124507 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8db2909b-26fd-53bf-8ce2-9fca4451efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Traces of Ellipsoids"}] :question/id #uuid "ecc934f5-9339-5076-b2d0-58b113364b54" :question/math-academy-id "e-5312" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the sphere $x^2 + (y+2)^2 + (z-3)^2 = 25?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2}+(0-3)^{2} & =25 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2}+9 & =25 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of the circle of radius $4$ centered at $(0,-2)$ in the $xy$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124506 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "304a85ac-e980-5081-8f2b-20df471c30fc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Center and Radius of a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99ff0bee-2eb2-50e8-87cd-b7fd103093fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398592} {:answer/id #uuid "72a9aeba-e4a8-5fb4-952f-d24c797294fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398593} {:answer/id #uuid "dd6ec8be-4e28-5339-a7f2-8fd7158128e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398594} {:answer/id #uuid "921a96a5-579d-5f70-be47-3cf461114085" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398595} {:answer/id #uuid "960900f4-7e67-5f08-869d-467271a2c7e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "921a96a5-579d-5f70-be47-3cf461114085" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398595} :answer-field/id #uuid "894e1641-4cda-5256-a33c-65967a2846fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398591}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16dea1c4-5f05-52d5-8897-db965a563c2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-164249" :question/problem "What is the radius of the sphere $(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-4z=12?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $y$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}-4z & =12 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+({z}^{2}-4z+4) & =12+4 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-2)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-2)^{2}={4}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us a radius of $4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284460 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124502 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Intercepts of Spheres and Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b97d1c4-3992-522e-9cad-586c7a80a6e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-16)$ and $(0,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281796} {:answer/id #uuid "6c3860ae-ebbf-5814-8765-0508616cef4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-1)$ and $(0,0,16)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282616} {:answer/id #uuid "897354ab-ef9e-5df5-92d9-20e1da7d7c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282878} {:answer/id #uuid "a19c5b13-a24a-51ac-b48f-69386e1c309e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,1)$ and $(0,0,16)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283099} {:answer/id #uuid "c19b9d20-03b2-5dca-985b-07007aa2653b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c19b9d20-03b2-5dca-985b-07007aa2653b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283372} :answer-field/id #uuid "e500241a-51ba-5ee0-8ecd-86ef5ccbaa3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "977b790d-d528-5cb6-b881-449f5c0f1471" :question/math-academy-id "q-164275" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{40}=1$, find its intercepts with the $z$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{40} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{10}+\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{40} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{z}^{2}}{40} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =16 \\\\ z & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-4$ and $z=4.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378913 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124502 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Intercepts of Spheres and Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fac58459-fc8a-5be9-a174-357811457c1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378915} {:answer/id #uuid "472da650-36fa-5f79-a933-0ba9360f241a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378916} {:answer/id #uuid "f82ff234-f117-517b-813c-c4767f7d1219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378917} {:answer/id #uuid "1b6cafc0-e998-5e08-8682-7a681d233ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-2)$ and $(0,0,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378918} {:answer/id #uuid "57202985-5772-5066-a73b-46c3a4f15432" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-1)$ and $(0,0,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "472da650-36fa-5f79-a933-0ba9360f241a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378916} :answer-field/id #uuid "a327b759-622d-5e88-8ad4-130e3ada74ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "316cb11c-48d9-5765-808b-1c4ae60a779c" :question/math-academy-id "q-164283" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{18}=1$, find its intercepts with the $z$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\$\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{18} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{18} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{z}^{2}}{18} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =9 \\\\ z & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-3$ and $z=3.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,3).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378927 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c2d581-8b12-575d-bb78-d8bb293a7339" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Sphere or Ellipsoid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abcc6672-0a4f-5b81-8a63-fc0d626dc112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $1$ centered at  $(\\sqrt{2},0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378929} {:answer/id #uuid "b898cbaf-984e-5450-bac2-8ece98fc9afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $1$ centered at  $(0,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378930} {:answer/id #uuid "73be320b-f16f-5598-b530-b59bfeb6a63e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $1$ centered at  $(0,-\\sqrt{2})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378931} {:answer/id #uuid "57e24ecf-a1c3-59cc-8ce7-6a64c874a62f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $2$ centered at  $(2,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378932} {:answer/id #uuid "bc1a7352-d96a-58b7-b7c5-9d347d7cb95e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $2$ centered at  $(-2,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57e24ecf-a1c3-59cc-8ce7-6a64c874a62f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $2$ centered at  $(2,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378932} :answer-field/id #uuid "f306b6b7-3d10-5b14-9eca-a2fd85fb47ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378928}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5fe8757-d817-5a49-b319-898d54ef3e7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-164308" :question/problem "Given the sphere $(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z+1)^{2}=4,$ what is the domain of $z=z(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the sphere, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z+1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =4-((x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{4-((x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2})} \\\\ z & =-1\\pm \\sqrt{4-((x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-((x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2})\\ge 0 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis inequality describes the interior and boundary of the circle \n\n$$\n(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4\n$$\n\nwhich is a circle of radius $2$ centered at $(2,0)$ in the $xy$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419596 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c2d581-8b12-575d-bb78-d8bb293a7339" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Sphere or Ellipsoid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab49ac7-5a6c-58cb-87a6-825f1cb8f419" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564955} {:answer/id #uuid "0d3c96ea-5670-502d-8704-137e6b80890c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564961} {:answer/id #uuid "214587ee-5a72-54a5-bc0e-f7077300d975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}>1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564989} {:answer/id #uuid "85156f66-70b0-5f66-992e-d91104d46a3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}<1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565146} {:answer/id #uuid "f2240426-8bf1-53c9-881b-8abf1853d3b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}>1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d3c96ea-5670-502d-8704-137e6b80890c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564961} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e468b59-ed57-5245-8552-ab699c4cd823" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419595}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "204288b8-790b-5fba-b88f-1aae9820b71f" :question/math-academy-id "q-164316" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}+(z-1)^{2}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the ellipsoid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}+(z-1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (z-1)^{2} & =1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} \\\\ z-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the interior of the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}=1$ and its boundary. \n\nTherefore, the domain is \n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}\\le 1\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c2d581-8b12-575d-bb78-d8bb293a7339" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Sphere or Ellipsoid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22760f57-3124-5878-9b94-278f7e5b10fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{10}<1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564991} {:answer/id #uuid "48abc19a-6b5d-5c36-b5d4-fc5eefeeb76e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{10}<1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565044} {:answer/id #uuid "6578a17f-6504-51fd-836a-0aaca0335274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565095} {:answer/id #uuid "84934c80-5b5a-533d-bf99-16c473356536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{10}<1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565145} {:answer/id #uuid "a517551e-b8df-5ff5-9c71-4f55e5aaf68a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{10}>1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6578a17f-6504-51fd-836a-0aaca0335274" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565095} :answer-field/id #uuid "eed84c94-e60c-5755-a59d-121744a369f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "52e8bd9d-8ee3-5485-a8a6-bac786018ef0" :question/math-academy-id "q-164317" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{5}=1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" :question/worked-solution "From the ellipsoid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{5} & =1 \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =5(1-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}-{y}^{2}) \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{5(1-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}-{y}^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}-{y}^{2}\\ge 0 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the interior of the ellipse $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+{y}^{2}=1$ and its boundary. \n\nTherefore, the domain is \n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+{y}^{2}\\le 1\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284477 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c2d581-8b12-575d-bb78-d8bb293a7339" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Sphere or Ellipsoid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e625bc8-a4f0-55f8-b453-92f6041add8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $9$ centered at $(3,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281962} {:answer/id #uuid "489bc5c0-5f54-5f70-97cd-aa938800d595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $3$ centered at $(-3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282304} {:answer/id #uuid "5138def5-d59a-5f50-89d4-35d223267a92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $9$ centered at $(-3,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282384} {:answer/id #uuid "989e0f17-b369-5205-b190-fa1092c5bee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(-3,4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283011} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e164f2-317e-57c2-83ee-264969da7739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $3$ centered at $(3,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "489bc5c0-5f54-5f70-97cd-aa938800d595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $3$ centered at $(-3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282304} :answer-field/id #uuid "d25b7f48-2f3f-5171-a3c9-931824f7ca3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6afd7b69-5cc1-5a73-9071-703e04661638" :question/math-academy-id "q-164378" :question/problem "Given the sphere $(x+3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}+(z-4)^{2}=9,$ what is the domain of $z=z(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the sphere, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}+(z-4)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (z-4)^{2} & =9-((x+3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}) \\\\ z-4 & =\\pm \\sqrt{9-({x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2})} \\\\ z & =4\\pm \\sqrt{9-((x+3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-((x+3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2})\\ge 0 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis inequality describes the interior and boundary of the circle \n\n$$\n(x+3)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=9\n$$\n\nwhich is a circle of radius $3$ centered at $(-3,1)$ in the $xy$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124649 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08c2d581-8b12-575d-bb78-d8bb293a7339" :knowledge-point/title "The Domain of a Sphere or Ellipsoid"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45942b3e-7799-54ff-a410-0f58ab63045a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$  centered at $(-1,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378950} {:answer/id #uuid "1b23f50d-db96-558b-9a20-f3bff7e2de44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $9$  centered at $(-1,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378951} {:answer/id #uuid "c771cfb3-d524-5543-a632-d7bd53cf11bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $3$  centered at $(1,-3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378952} {:answer/id #uuid "58d01120-1590-5fae-8170-2ae5adc67488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $3$  centered at $(-3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378953} {:answer/id #uuid "a23cb399-96ed-5aab-84ef-fe776b4a6cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$  centered at $(-3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45942b3e-7799-54ff-a410-0f58ab63045a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The interior and boundary of the circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$  centered at $(-1,3)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378950} :answer-field/id #uuid "721dfe8e-a6a9-5d59-8652-74c44e2da19a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6423dc93-7d2d-540e-980c-bc6677e7ca75" :question/math-academy-id "q-164402" :question/problem "Given the sphere $(x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}+(z+3)^{2}=3,$ what is the domain of $z=z(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the sphere, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}+(z+3)^{2} & =3 \\\\ (z+3)^{2} & =3-((x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}) \\\\ z+3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{3-((x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2})} \\\\ z & =-3\\pm \\sqrt{3-((x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the square root is defined only for non-negative arguments, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-((x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2})\\ge 0 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis inequality describes the interior and boundary of the circle \n\n$$\n(x+1)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=3\n$$\n\nwhich is a circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(-1,3)$ in the $xy$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565460 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124502 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Intercepts of Spheres and Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26ab3ac5-f520-5775-ae79-28d69c2b721d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-2,0)$ and $(0,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564999} {:answer/id #uuid "322693c6-801e-530e-a07a-0cf0972d13fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-\\frac{2}{5},0)$ and $(0,-\\frac{8}{5},0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565015} {:answer/id #uuid "3b62ac1c-ec02-5ef6-83c0-b9d4f5799d95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,\\frac{3}{10},0)$ and $(0,-\\frac{3}{10},0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565024} {:answer/id #uuid "92f1d345-9338-572b-a022-a2aa7c192bc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,\\frac{1}{5},0)$ and $(0,-\\frac{3}{5},0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565161} {:answer/id #uuid "94022cd2-8c4f-5fd7-b797-94b3f7dfe921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,2,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26ab3ac5-f520-5775-ae79-28d69c2b721d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-2,0)$ and $(0,0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564999} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4183e30-864f-59d2-a111-26fabe8674fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be1595d6-b16a-5715-995c-d3645afe8a1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-64729" :question/problem "Given the ellipse $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{2}=1$, find its intercepts with the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{10} & =\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =1 \\\\ y+1 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ y & =-1\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $y=-2$ and $y=0.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-2,0)$ and $(0,0,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565458 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124507 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8db2909b-26fd-53bf-8ce2-9fca4451efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Traces of Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00ddf948-b4f2-5570-a9a2-cfeb90393262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564940} {:answer/id #uuid "214e9af2-9dcc-58c5-a4b5-fda2774bf47b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564990} {:answer/id #uuid "584822f5-08a3-58ab-b2e2-b93186d19784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+{z}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565075} {:answer/id #uuid "60315c93-1ed6-5daa-b8f2-20d4ac6ba748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565085} {:answer/id #uuid "9424b3f7-d0f0-5bce-803a-28321ac7f675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60315c93-1ed6-5daa-b8f2-20d4ac6ba748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565085} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa0cb4b6-a616-5b8f-b534-fcf340469087" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b46dd9b0-6a80-5531-9884-f4687e775cb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-70487" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(0)^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124506 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "304a85ac-e980-5081-8f2b-20df471c30fc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Center and Radius of a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a580078-e0be-51b6-94bb-711d36dd9c97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=\\sqrt{2}$ and $C(0,3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336581} {:answer/id #uuid "63e97839-5c2c-5770-96d1-ed8f376fa3cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=2$ and $C(0,-3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336930} {:answer/id #uuid "9b16af0c-b883-50cf-87aa-6a2932ae43c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=\\sqrt{2}$ and $C(0,3,-1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337438} {:answer/id #uuid "b856bccd-c706-5261-93e0-497f373d6ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=\\sqrt{2}$ and $C(0,-3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337666} {:answer/id #uuid "df411767-3d5e-548b-afbe-b84db693ab01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=2$ and $C(0,3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b856bccd-c706-5261-93e0-497f373d6ae5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$r=\\sqrt{2}$ and $C(0,-3,1)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337666} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c715456-3e4f-525b-95c5-122bd2ea0f3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338535}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fdb4f6bd-92de-5fb3-a5cc-3d88dfc3947f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70560" :question/problem "What are the radius $r$ and the coordinates of the center $C$ for the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=2?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can write our equation as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2}+(z-1)^{2}=(\\sqrt{2})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the center at the point point $C(0,-3,1)$ and the radius $r=\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124506 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "304a85ac-e980-5081-8f2b-20df471c30fc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Center and Radius of a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "151f846f-5e15-5b61-a5a2-618ae7d7dc76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336233} {:answer/id #uuid "3ae090f5-9163-56ef-bf69-c7fb24120d3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336585} {:answer/id #uuid "41d70b71-3382-50e6-93c5-908817beed77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336652} {:answer/id #uuid "6f537ce7-1659-586e-8f53-0f89142a6f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337018} {:answer/id #uuid "eb81a84a-ce20-55c8-bdde-9be71292c699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb81a84a-ce20-55c8-bdde-9be71292c699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338087} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3a5826c-891b-5f14-965f-01e705656109" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6b356f6b-9965-5431-ba35-16fc873edc26" :question/math-academy-id "q-70563" :question/problem "What is the radius of the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+6y+(z-1)^{2}=16?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $y$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+6y+(z-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}+6y+9)+(z-1)^{2} & =16+9 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+(z-1)^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2}+(z-1)^{2}={5}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us a radius of $5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379875 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124506 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "304a85ac-e980-5081-8f2b-20df471c30fc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Center and Radius of a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c6e34a6-3002-50e5-932b-1a70890b2fe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379877} {:answer/id #uuid "9de3fa78-b033-587c-a692-bced7f267128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379878} {:answer/id #uuid "45876beb-fab3-5e26-a3ca-4911a198ebfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379879} {:answer/id #uuid "f62f10ca-0b4a-5adc-996e-33919e4fe001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379880} {:answer/id #uuid "2c1bc22d-651a-5388-a472-cf0bd977f8ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9de3fa78-b033-587c-a692-bced7f267128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379878} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfd8d4bc-cf7c-544d-9e68-9c0791294d97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dc3dada1-2402-5dbc-9284-d0f3206acefa" :question/math-academy-id "q-70651" :question/problem "What is the radius of the sphere $(x+3)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}+{z}^{2}-10z=24?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $z$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}+{z}^{2}-10z & =24 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}+({z}^{2}-10z+25) & =24+25 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}+(z-5)^{2} & =49\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x+3)^{2}+(y-4)^{2}+(z-5)^{2}={7}^{2}\n$$\n\nwhich gives us a radius of $7.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124507 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8db2909b-26fd-53bf-8ce2-9fca4451efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Traces of Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "441ad13a-04d3-57c6-a04e-0fc82c408cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(0,4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403421} {:answer/id #uuid "341432ad-44c3-5414-b4d8-57e378337db7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $12$ centered at $(0,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403422} {:answer/id #uuid "826e586e-0569-5bb6-96de-10fe4b4015a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $2$ centered at $(0,-4)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403423} {:answer/id #uuid "9c58bd12-17f3-5565-aa62-7cb54d35d4f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $4$ centered at $(4,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403424} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d92dd1-4df6-5c59-877d-4394830adaba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $2\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(-4,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7d92dd1-4df6-5c59-877d-4394830adaba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $2\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(-4,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403425} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c3aa403-fc33-5342-8a02-494977341c7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1624d2db-d10f-59ae-bae3-c241890eb9fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-70926" :question/problem "What is the projection of the intersection between the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2}=16$ and the plane $x=2$ onto the $yz$-plane." :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the sphere and the plane $x=2$, we substitute $x=2$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 4+(y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =16 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =12 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProjecting this onto the $yz$-plane gives us the circle of radius $2\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(-4,0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124507 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8db2909b-26fd-53bf-8ce2-9fca4451efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Traces of Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30dd4ed5-27e6-55f9-8a61-c0c123215d0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336499} {:answer/id #uuid "51defa3d-5086-5470-9a14-402b8ff185c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336783} {:answer/id #uuid "6c0775f8-42d1-536c-982f-7f0eea4bb65d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}+(z+2)^{2}=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336988} {:answer/id #uuid "847620d2-6755-5a12-8c91-89fb08087da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}+(z-2)^{2}=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337227} {:answer/id #uuid "9002f906-cd83-5895-8cc9-e7ecc7bb5f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(z+2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9002f906-cd83-5895-8cc9-e7ecc7bb5f3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(z+2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337336} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8c36c22-20de-517a-84c2-f1d6d84aa45d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338712}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "863e5eab-b375-5fa8-afc8-dc170a1abcfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-70927" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the sphere $(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z+2)^{2}=16?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(z+2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(z+2)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124506 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "304a85ac-e980-5081-8f2b-20df471c30fc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Center and Radius of a Sphere"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0973e9ca-e0a7-571c-a8f0-019ff57826b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564954} {:answer/id #uuid "5533b44b-f929-586d-b63a-eb6b4676aff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565063} {:answer/id #uuid "8b926eb0-063a-5a1d-8cbb-886a18b3afe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565153} {:answer/id #uuid "cdd35525-6aa6-5770-8013-b818e7e4d6b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565245} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3cec0d-40d3-5e91-911a-bbaee6095b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed3cec0d-40d3-5e91-911a-bbaee6095b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565293} :answer-field/id #uuid "09bef14a-87dd-54de-aa74-0d9d9cab649d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e09cfecd-e23b-5baa-8f4c-7e2b5c69c1a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-71945" :question/problem "What is the radius of the sphere ${x}^{2}-6x+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=17?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nBy completing the square for the variable $x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-6x+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =17 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-6x+9)+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =17+9 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=(\\sqrt{26})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us a radius of $\\sqrt{26}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124507 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8db2909b-26fd-53bf-8ce2-9fca4451efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Traces of Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81ee28c2-2985-581b-8e4f-846f188976a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $\\sqrt{5}$ centered at $(0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337214} {:answer/id #uuid "a716f8fb-2807-5197-8616-199b41c26567" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $6$ centered at $(0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337544} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ba2520-ca20-55e4-ab5c-8f7dbecccb1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $2\\sqrt{5}$ centered at $(0,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337636} {:answer/id #uuid "c9505a17-d88e-595c-b6a3-ee7ceba8ad55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $20$ centered at $(0,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337811} {:answer/id #uuid "d7277dc5-3ba0-5360-8674-c6513318a0cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $2\\sqrt{5}$ centered at $(0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7277dc5-3ba0-5360-8674-c6513318a0cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The circle of radius $2\\sqrt{5}$ centered at $(0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337900} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ba416b5-5daf-5e81-b6d8-4eac8b41622c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338326}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6659b2ae-532f-58c0-9b8a-93e7c4f9a624" :question/math-academy-id "q-71949" :question/problem "What is the projection of the intersection between the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+(z+1)^{2}=36$ and the plane $z=3$ onto the $xy$-plane." :question/worked-solution "To find the intersection of the sphere and the plane $z=3$, we substitute $z=3$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+(3+1)^{2} & =36 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+16 & =36 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{5})^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProjecting this onto the $xy$-plane gives us the equation of the circle of radius $2\\sqrt{5}$ centered at $(0,2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124502 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Intercepts of Spheres and Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11794d75-cf96-590e-bdca-c3183edad1d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-\\frac{16}{9},0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339281} {:answer/id #uuid "13c76fe1-8968-5eaf-94ce-0c784c590365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-\\frac{4}{3},0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339303} {:answer/id #uuid "247b300f-eb84-5cfa-bb3a-7eba5f99e1d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-2,0)$ and $(0,2,0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339444} {:answer/id #uuid "7f35e3af-4c69-5f9c-8224-b42028bb64b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-\\frac{8}{3},0)$ and $(0,-\\frac{4}{3},0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340271} {:answer/id #uuid "bec8e0f2-6c92-5f29-aadc-1e46151bb7ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,-\\frac{4}{3},0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f35e3af-4c69-5f9c-8224-b42028bb64b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,-\\frac{8}{3},0)$ and $(0,-\\frac{4}{3},0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340271} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d8db404-8b1b-5e5c-8e2e-d91558bd3be8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "92b5bb6f-415d-5913-8624-6ebb244cd292" :question/math-academy-id "q-73214" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{9}+(y+2)^{2}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{9}=1$, find its intercepts with the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0+1)^{2}}{9}+(y+2)^{2}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}+(y+2)^{2}+\\frac{4}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{5}{9}+(y+2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ (y+2)^{2} & =\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ y+2 & =\\pm \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ y & =-2\\pm \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $y=-\\frac{8}{3}$ and $y=-\\frac{4}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-\\frac{8}{3},0)$ and $(0,-\\frac{4}{3},0).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124502 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "64e7d2fb-003c-58c0-ab80-159e50748cc7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Intercepts of Spheres and Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92574954-56db-5e22-8577-4044312d87ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,0,\\frac{5}{2})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393287} {:answer/id #uuid "d26ac35c-3433-55c1-aba9-04ac4fb4be37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ and $(0,0,\\frac{5}{2})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393288} {:answer/id #uuid "da7d850c-c7da-5536-9a3e-8dfd4dedca68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,0,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393289} {:answer/id #uuid "9f21d78c-dfb5-5f80-8f9d-1894eb115cb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,\\frac{9}{4})$ and $(0,0,\\frac{7}{4})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393290} {:answer/id #uuid "1d2f6bf3-3c38-5c3a-982b-11d71b8fcc1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,\\frac{5}{2})$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d26ac35c-3433-55c1-aba9-04ac4fb4be37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(0,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ and $(0,0,\\frac{5}{2})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393288} :answer-field/id #uuid "4865ffc5-356e-5dc2-8e39-a104fadf276d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "968294df-641c-514f-b1fc-74e1ba659362" :question/math-academy-id "q-73215" :question/problem "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{12}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{2}=1$, find its intercepts with the $z$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-3)^{2}}{12}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{7}{8}+\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ (z-2)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ z-2 & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ z & =2\\pm \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=\\frac{3}{2}$ and $z=\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ and $(0,0,\\frac{5}{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186565414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124507 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8db2909b-26fd-53bf-8ce2-9fca4451efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Traces of Ellipsoids"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "003023dc-51c9-58e2-b59b-9f0ea7d84f7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An ellipse with semi-axes $6$ and $12,$ centered at $(1,-1)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564938} {:answer/id #uuid "1f892faa-9f38-5185-b735-5e66823a7dd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An ellipse with semi-axes $\\sqrt{6}$ and $12,$ centered at $(1,1)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564987} {:answer/id #uuid "2316a495-6ef9-5785-8b09-333b0185ce24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An ellipse with semi-axes $\\sqrt{6}$ and $2\\sqrt{3},$ centered at $(1,-1)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564992} {:answer/id #uuid "bc922231-524b-5a1a-85e8-999ef648b749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An ellipse with semi-axes $\\sqrt{6}$ and $2\\sqrt{3},$ centered at $(-1,1)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565223} {:answer/id #uuid "f48baf3b-f02e-5d1c-8183-91b15a183361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An ellipse with semi-axes $6$ and $2\\sqrt{3},$ centered at $(1,-1)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc922231-524b-5a1a-85e8-999ef648b749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "An ellipse with semi-axes $\\sqrt{6}$ and $2\\sqrt{3},$ centered at $(-1,1)$ in the $yz$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565223} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dae42d3-3f69-5f16-a665-8518e5d1111c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "15b3432d-8b0c-5d62-a84d-7dadd72f7ac7" :question/math-academy-id "q-73216" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{12}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the ellipsoid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{12}=1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{12}=1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of the ellipse with semi-axes $\\sqrt{6}$ and $2\\sqrt{3},$ centered at $(-1,1)$ in the $yz$-plane."}]}
